WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.979
The final episodes of fan favorite TV shows
tend to be emotional, from sadness, to a sense

00:00:05.979 --> 00:00:10.960
of closure, and even to anger over things
not panning out quite as audiences may have

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:11.960
expected.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.190
In the case of these shows, though, the major
feeling most fans got after watching their

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:17.670
final moments was total confusion.

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:21.840
Here are some TV show endings that required
a little unpacking.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.510
The Sopranos

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:28.460
Perhaps the most perplexing TV finale of all
time, The Sopranos' final scene is still nothing

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.020
short of confounding.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:35.680
Throughout the last season, fans picked apart
every episode, theorizing about how the story

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.910
of mafia boss Tony Soprano would conclude,
but chances are, nobody saw this coming.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:45.380
In the final moments, the show's anti-hero
and his family are shown sitting at a diner,

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:49.840
listening to Journey's "Don't Stop Believin',"
before Tony notices a man looking around the

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:51.300
diner and….

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.120
"Don't stop..."

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:58.280
The quickfire curtaining was so abrupt that
many viewers thought something went wrong

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:02.970
with their cable feed, and when they realized
it wasn't a technical error, they were fuming

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:03.970
even more.

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:07.780
According to series creator David Chase, the
ending was meant to imply that Tony would

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:12.390
always be paranoid, and that endings for guys
like him usually come out of nowhere like

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:13.390
this.

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:17.929
But it's taken fans years of dissection to
draw their own conclusions about Tony's ultimate

00:01:17.929 --> 00:01:21.619
fate, and even still, not everyone's convinced
it was conclusive.

00:01:21.619 --> 00:01:26.499
It was a huge letdown for what was otherwise
a legendary series.

00:01:26.499 --> 00:01:27.909
Roseanne

00:01:27.909 --> 00:01:32.440
For eight seasons, Roseanne brought the midwestern
blue collar life to light by way of the Conner

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:33.440
family.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:37.270
From their consistent money troubles to their
kids' disappointing decisions, the sitcom

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:42.829
series was underscored by some relatable drama
that carried it for nearly a decade without

00:01:42.829 --> 00:01:43.829
issue.

00:01:43.829 --> 00:01:48.349
But then in the ninth and once-final season,
the Connors came into some serious dough after

00:01:48.349 --> 00:01:52.490
winning the lottery, and the show went completely
off the rails.

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:57.130
The last run quickly turned into some Beverly
Hillbillies redux that featured Dan having

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:02.079
an affair, Darlene delivering a premature
baby, and a massive last-minute twist that

00:02:02.079 --> 00:02:03.929
basically erased it all.

00:02:03.929 --> 00:02:07.679
In the final moments, we find out the whole
series was a book written by Roseanne.

00:02:07.679 --> 00:02:12.099
But she's taken some creative liberties to
cope with and escape her harsh realities.

00:02:12.099 --> 00:02:16.239
Notably, Dan hadn't had an affair…because
he'd died from a heart attack years before.

00:02:16.239 --> 00:02:20.970
And as a result of that switcheroo, she proceeds
to explain that much of the events seen on

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:24.530
the show never happened, like who her kids
actually married.

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:29.519
The wonky ending was not well-received, and
with a Roseanne revival en route for 2018,

00:02:29.519 --> 00:02:34.340
we can probably count on that backtracking
to take another drastic turn as John Goodman

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:36.750
is reprising his role for the new series.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:41.370
As far as we know, he's not expected to return
as some zombie, no matter how much the Conner

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:43.280
family loved their Halloween tricks.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:45.280
"Let me look at you, you're gonna need stitches.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:46.280
AHHH!"

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:51.700
So, chances are, the finale will get swept
under the rug altogether by the time the new

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:52.980
series launches.

00:03:01.849 --> 00:03:03.579
Battlestar Galactica

00:03:03.579 --> 00:03:08.930
With Battlestar Galactica, the Syfy channel
took the classic, 1970s show about space hippies

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:13.739
and turned it into a gritty story about the
last humans trying to survive in outer space.

00:03:13.739 --> 00:03:18.180
The show featured humans that were from another
galaxy, venturing out into space looking for

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:21.220
the lost human colony of Earth to make a new
home there.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:25.109
In the last season, they finally find the
third rock from the sun, but it's a nuclear

00:03:25.109 --> 00:03:27.330
wasteland and everyone is dead.

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:32.079
The confusion sets in when we see Kara "Starbuck"
Thrace return from the dead under mysterious

00:03:32.079 --> 00:03:35.330
circumstances to usher them into their new
dwelling.

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:40.159
She'd seemingly passed away in the prior season,
so her ill-explained revival was a head-scratcher

00:03:40.159 --> 00:03:41.159
indeed.

00:03:41.159 --> 00:03:45.920
But then things got even more inexplicable
when, in the finale, she is shown saying goodbye

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:48.999
to Apollo before disappearing into the wind.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.300
"I'm done here.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:54.360
I've completed my journey."

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:58.329
Executive producer Ron Moore tried to explain
that Starbuck had been brought back to life

00:03:58.329 --> 00:04:03.230
by a higher power to lead the humans to Earth,
but real-life Earthlings were left stunned

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:05.620
by the bizarre stunt.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:06.620
Hannibal

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:11.579
Bryan Fuller's stylish horror series took
the idea of a cliffhanger literally.

00:04:11.579 --> 00:04:16.000
The show's murderous cannibal Hannibal Lecter
and FBI profiler Will Graham culminate their

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:21.170
twisted, series-long game of cat and mouse
with a brutal combat at the edge of a cliff,

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:25.110
at which point they both fall off into the
sea … and that's it.

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:29.470
We're left to wonder whether anyone survived
the fall, and the question mark about that

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:32.850
prospect is even furthered by the Season 3
post-credits scene.

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:37.980
In it, Hannibal's enabler psychiatrist Bedelia
is shown waiting at a dinner table with two

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:42.280
empty place settings, and her own severed
leg ready to be served.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:44.850
Kinda makes you hungry for more, no?

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.060
Angel

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:51.560
When this spinoff of Buffy the Vampire Slayer
debuted in 1999, it was about vampire Angel's

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:54.360
small Los Angeles private detective agency.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:58.040
By the end of the fifth season, however, the
show had evolved into a story of a grand war

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:02.160
between good and evil, in which Angel and
his cohorts were determined to destroy the

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:04.470
wicked Circle of the Black Thorn.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:08.382
The final shots of the series finale show
Angel and the good guys heading into a battle

00:05:08.382 --> 00:05:12.230
against a massive army—just as the episode
ends.

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:16.061
Ending in the beginning of a battle is certainly
an understandable point of confusion, but

00:05:16.061 --> 00:05:20.060
co-creator Joss Whedon told TV Guide that
the final scene of the series demonstrates

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:23.950
the notion that the war between good and evil
is never over, saying,

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:26.810
"The point of the show is that you're never
done.

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:29.280
No matter who goes down, the fight goes on."

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:32.580
And so does the fan quest for a sense of closure
…

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:36.040
"Then let's make 'em memorable."

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:37.960
Thanks for watching!

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:40.480
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:42.750
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

